+// Browser process only. Refuses DevTools and every CDP attach for this launch.
+//
+// A switch and NOT a config key, deliberately. The fingerprint config describes
+// a persona — what the profile claims to be — and it is republished into shared
+// memory for every child process including renderers. This is not a claim about
+// a machine, it is a restriction on an operator, and the two must not share a
+// channel. argv also has the property this needs: it is fixed when the browser
+// starts and nothing running inside the profile can change it afterwards, while
+// a preference lives in a JSON file inside the user-data-dir that anyone with
+// the unpacked profile can edit between launches.
+//
+// What it does not stop, stated plainly because a restriction whose limits are
+// undocumented gets trusted past them: an operator who has the binary can
+// relaunch it by hand without this switch. That is the threat model in
+// docs/04 — a dishonest employee with the profile, not one with root on the
+// machine.
+COMPONENT_EXPORT(FURY) extern const char kLockDevTools[];
+
 }  // namespace switches
 }  // namespace fury
 
